    # and its close-out rulings, and grepped for part 6's names, paths, commit
    # ids and typed counts. What differs from that one, and why:
    #  1. The phase, the log directory and the status terms are part 7 P1's
    #     (records/logs/m1p7-p1; P1 has no record pair); the previous phase's
    #     figures and names are read from records/logs/m1p6-p3/test.log.
    #  2. The commits by role: the part 6 close-out record commit (the base),
    #     the first doc commit, the second doc commit and the code commit (the
    #     phase commit), each resolved by its subject with a printed command and
    #     checked against the phase commit's parents. No id is typed.
    #  3. P1 changes tools/xlsx-diff alone, so the core-only blocks of part 6
    #     P3 are dropped: the library's per-module tests, the core with the dates
    #     feature off and on, clippy on the core, the emend-copy tool's
    #     null_rewrite binary, the size-probe builds, the probe and its PM
    #     mutations, and C1's and C2's claims. The workspace runs on both targets
    #     still run every test of every crate.
    #  4. New blocks: xlsx-diff's p7 tests and its unit tests by name on both
    #     targets; the case map of "### P1" and the rulings; ruling 8's
    #     measurement (a probe planted in the worktree's compare_xml records the
    #     test thread of every comparison that prints xml rows, over p1 to p6,
    #     with p7 as the control; then p3.rs reverted to the base under the new
    #     helpers shows which pre-existing test needs more than the helpers);
    #     the mutations M1 to M10 of the comparison, each expected to fail a
    #     named test, a mutation that does not is printed as a FINDING; the code
    #     commit's claims.
    #  5. The target directory is named once, as <scratch>/p1/target, the same
    #     in this header and in the body (specs/0013 P1 verification ruling 6).
    #     Each second root has one header line saying which spelled path stands
    #     for it and that the roots are distinct (P2 verification ruling 5); the
    #     SERIALIZED line carries the process count (P2 verification ruling 6).
    #  6. Everything else is part 6 P3's final form: lines 1 to 3 are the
    #     command, the invocation and "about:"; then the three shape greps over
    #     this script with their controls; the by-name comparison with the
    #     previous log; the added tests derived from the source; the ignored
    #     tests derived from the source; the comparison of the two targets. The
    #     counts this log prints are read from the runs, never typed.
    #  7. None of the three shapes specs/0001 forbids appears here; the shapes
    #     are described rather than written out.
    #  8. Attempt 2 (after attempt 1, named in the rerun line below): the
    #     mutation block counted cargo's own "error: test failed" and "error: 1
    #     target failed" summary lines as build errors, so attempt 1 printed
    #     every mutation as a FINDING while its failing-test lists showed the
    #     named test failing. A build failure is now cargo's "could not compile"
    #     line, with a control; a bite-mode mutation that does not bite now fails
    #     its check; M9 on the host is MEASURED (the framing argument in the
    #     block). Nothing else changed.
    #  9. Rerun at the second code commit (planning's message after independent
