## what the second code commit's message claims (header change 9)
    M1 part 7 P1: line ends across markup, and the fixtures check 1 asked for
    
    Independent check 1 (F1) found that the text node's CR state crossed a
    comment, a processing instruction or a CDATA delimiter, so a CR before
    one and an LF after it read as one line end. They are not adjacent in
    the document, so under XML 1.0 section 2.11 they are two. Text::markup
    now ends the CR state at each of them, and the Limits say so. The
    Limits also say that a text node a parse error interrupts is never
    hashed, so a raw reference in it is not counted (check 1 F4).
    
    Tests added to tests/p7.rs: a CR, a comment and an LF, and a CR ending
    a CDATA section then an LF, each equal to two LFs; a CR, a comment and
    an LF against one LF, which differs; a byte order mark on one side; an
    xml:space attribute resolving to the XML namespace; an added entry's
    row standing before the first xml row (check 1 F2, F3); the derivation
    of the offsets 15 and 18 in a comment (F13). Whether the new tests
    fail without the fix is shown in this phase's test.log, not by this
    message.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
